          <p>
            Bloom lists Clear Protein at about $30 per pouch, with discounts on two- and three-pouch bundles. We could not confirm the number of servings per pouch from Bloom's materials at the time of writing, so check the label before you compare it with other clear proteins. Whatever the servings count, remember that you are paying for 20 g of protein of which 15 g is whey.
          </p>

          <p>
            For comparison, a large tub of a mainstream isolate bought on sale often lands around $1.30 to $1.70 per 25 g. A one-shake-a-day habit with Bloom therefore costs roughly $5 to $15 a month more than the cheaper option. That is not a dealbreaker if you love the flavor, but it is real money over a year, and it buys you no extra certification.
          </p>

          <p>
            Bloom's bundles and subscriptions can narrow the gap. If you are going to buy it anyway, buying a multi-pack or subscribing is the cheapest way in. If you are on a tight budget, our <a href="/best-cheap-protein-powder/">best cheap protein powder</a> guide lists the tubs with the lowest cost per 25 g.
          </p>
