        <div id="faq" class="scroll-mt-24 mt-16">
          <h2 class="text-3xl font-black text-gray-900 mb-6">
            12. Frequently Asked Questions
          </h2>

          <div class="faq-list">
            <details class="faq-item">
              <summary><h3>Is Bloom protein powder good?</h3></summary>
              <div class="faq-answer">
                <p>
                  It is a reasonable product with popular flavors, but it is not standout. The Whey Isolate lists about 22 g of protein per scoop with a digestive enzyme blend, which is solid. It costs more per 25 g than mainstream isolates and carries no advertised sport certification, so it is best for people who specifically like Bloom's flavors and branding.
                </p>
              </div>
            </details>

            <details class="faq-item">
              <summary><h3>How much protein is in Bloom Whey Isolate?</h3></summary>
              <div class="faq-answer">
                <p>
                  About 22 g of protein per scoop, with the scoop weighing roughly 27.5 to 31 g depending on flavor, per labels at the time of writing. Calories are around 100 per scoop in nutrition-database listings of the label. Check the tub you buy, because sodium and exact macros vary from flavor to flavor.
                </p>
              </div>
            </details>

            <details class="faq-item">
              <summary><h3>Does Bloom Clear Protein contain collagen?</h3></summary>
              <div class="faq-answer">
                <p>
                  Yes. Bloom states each serving contains 15 g of whey protein isolate and 5 g of grass-fed collagen peptides, for 20 g of protein in total. Collagen is an incomplete protein that is low in leucine, so for muscle building the drink behaves more like a 15 g whey serving than a 20 g one.
                </p>
              </div>
            </details>

            <details class="faq-item">
              <summary><h3>What sweetener is in Bloom protein?</h3></summary>
              <div class="faq-answer">
                <p>
                  The Bloom Whey Isolate label we found for Iced Coffee lists sucralose and acesulfame potassium, and some reviewers also report stevia in the formula. Sweeteners can differ by flavor and formula version, so check the ingredient list on the tub. If you avoid artificial sweeteners, a stevia-only or unflavored isolate is the better choice.
                </p>
              </div>
            </details>

            <details class="faq-item">
              <summary><h3>Is Bloom protein third-party tested?</h3></summary>
              <div class="faq-answer">
                <p>
                  Bloom does not advertise NSF Certified for Sport, Informed Choice or Informed Sport status for its protein at the time of writing. That does not mean it is unsafe, but there is no public certification to verify. Drug-tested athletes should choose a certified product and confirm the exact flavor in the certifier's database.
                </p>
              </div>
            </details>

            <details class="faq-item">
              <summary><h3>Can I buy Bloom protein on Amazon?</h3></summary>
              <div class="faq-answer">
                <p>
                  Bloom's greens and energy products are widely sold on Amazon, but its protein is mainly sold through Bloom's own site and, for Clear Protein, Target. If you find Bloom whey on Amazon, check that the seller is Bloom Nutrition or Amazon, and compare the price with Bloom's site, because some resale listings cost noticeably more.
                </p>
              </div>
            </details>

            <details class="faq-item">
              <summary><h3>What is a better alternative to Bloom protein?</h3></summary>
              <div class="faq-answer">
                <p>
                  For more protein per dollar, Dymatize ISO100 lists about 25 g of protein per scoop, states Informed Choice certification, and is usually cheaper per 25 g. For a clear protein without collagen, Myprotein Clear Whey Isolate delivers about 20 g from whey isolate alone. Our whey isolate rankings list further options at different prices.
                </p>
              </div>
            </details>

